    '_p_style_text_align_justify_span_style_color_rgb_255_255_255_Kajian_terhadap_historiografi_Kabupaten_Garut_menyajikan_sebuah_diskursus_yang_sangat_mendalam_dan_multidimensional_mengenai_bagaimana_sebuah_entitas_administratif_di_wilayah_dataran_tinggi_Priangan_Jawa_Barat_bertransformasi_melewati_berbagai_epos_sejarah_yang_krusial_dan_bergejolak_Garut_bukan_sekadar_wilayah_penyangga_geografis_yang_pasif_ia_merupakan_episentrum_yang_secara_aktif_berpartisipasi_dalam_berbagai_peristiwa_lintas_negara_mulai_dari_penetrasi_awal_era_kolonialisme_Hindia_Belanda_periode_komodifikasi_pariwisata_global_pada_awal_abad_ke_20_palagan_revolusi_fisik_kemerdekaan_yang_berdarah_hingga_fase_konsolidasi_identitas_nasional_pasca_kolonial_span_br_p_' => '<p style="text-align: justify; "><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">The study of the historiography of Garut Regency presents a very in-depth and multidimensional discourse regarding how an administrative entity in the Priangan highlands region, West Java, was transformed through various crucial and turbulent historical epochs. Garut is not just a passive geographical buffer area; it is an epicenter that actively participates in various transnational events, starting from the initial penetration of the Dutch East Indies era of colonialism, the period of global tourism commodification at the beginning of the 20th century, the bloody physical revolution of independence, to the post-colonial national identity consolidation phase.</span><br /></p>',
    'Api_Revolusi_di_Dataran_Tinggi_Priangan' => 'Flames of Revolution in the Priangan Highlands',
    'Revitalisasi_Peran_Garut_Pasca_Bumi_Hangus_Bandung_Lautan_Api_1946_' => 'Revitalization of the Role of Garut Post-Scorched Earth "Bandung Lautan Api" (1946)',
    '_p_style_text_align_left_Peristiwa_monumental_span_style_font_weight_bold_Bandung_Lautan_Api_span_yang_meletus_pada_23_Maret_1946_memaksa_ratusan_ribu_penduduk_sipil_bersama_barisan_Tentara_Republik_Indonesia_TRI_untuk_membumihanguskan_infrastruktur_kota_Bandung_Taktik_drastis_ini_bertujuan_agar_kekuatan_militer_Sekutu_dan_rezim_NICA_tidak_dapat_memanfaatkan_fasilitas_strategis_tersebut_Gelombang_eksodus_dan_armada_laskar_pejuang_terpaksa_mundur_secara_taktis_ke_wilayah_selatan_yang_secara_instan_menempatkan_Kabupaten_Garut_sebagai_basis_benteng_pertahanan_utama_dan_komando_pusat_operasi_perang_gerilya_Lanskap_topografi_pegunungan_Garut_yang_terjal_berfungsi_sebagai_pelindung_benteng_alami_bagi_laskar_pejuang_termasuk_di_dalamnya_kekuatan_milisi_Laskar_Hizbullah_dalam_menyusun_dan_melancarkan_serangan_balasan_yang_asimetris_demi_mempertahankan_kedaulatan_kemerdekaan_Indonesia_br_p_' => '<p style="text-align: left;">The monumental event "<span style="font-weight: bold;">Bandung Lautan Api</span>" which erupted on March 23 1946 forced hundreds of thousands of civilians along with ranks of the Indonesian Republic Army (TRI) to burn down the infrastructure of the city of Bandung. This drastic tactic was aimed at preventing Allied military forces and the NICA regime from utilizing these strategic facilities. The wave of exodus and the army\'s fleet of fighters were forced to retreat tactically to the southern region, which instantly placed Garut Regency as the main defensive base and command center for guerrilla warfare operations. The steep topographic landscape of Garut\'s mountains serves as a natural fortress protection for the fighting forces—including the Laskar Hezbollah militia force—in preparing and launching asymmetrical counterattacks to defend Indonesia\'s independent sovereignty.<br /></p>',
    'Wajah_Klasik_Garut_Tata_Ruang_dan_Anatomi_Kekuasaan' => 'The Classic Face of Garut: Spatial Planning and Anatomy of Power',
    'Dinamika_Kehidupan_di_Alun_Alun_Garut_pada_Era_Hindia_Belanda_1890_1920_' => 'Dynamics of Life in Garut Square in the Dutch East Indies Era (1890-1920)',
    '_p_style_text_align_justify_Sejarah_pembentukan_Kabupaten_Garut_mencerminkan_dinamika_administratif_yang_kompleks_dengan_rujukan_pembentukan_wilayah_antara_tahun_1813_hingga_pembangunan_Jembatan_Leuwidaun_pada_1918_Dokumen_arsip_visual_dari_pergantian_abad_ke_20_memperlihatkan_Alun_alun_Garut_bukan_sekadar_ruang_kosong_melainkan_pusat_interaksi_sosial_politik_dan_keagamaan_yang_krusial_Di_kawasan_ini_terintegrasi_bangunan_bersejarah_Babancong_Masjid_Agung_Garut_kediaman_resmi_Bupati_hingga_monumen_kolonial_K_F_Holle_Dengan_latar_belakang_siluet_megah_Gunung_Cikuray_tata_ruang_ini_merepresentasikan_perpaduan_yang_sarat_makna_antara_sistem_kosmologi_pemerintahan_tradisional_Sunda_dan_intervensi_arsitektural_pemerintah_kolonial_br_p_' => '<p style="text-align: justify;">The history of the formation of Garut Regency reflects complex administrative dynamics, with references to the formation of the region between 1813 and the construction of the Leuwidaun Bridge in 1918. Visual archival documents from the turn of the 20th century show that Garut Square was not just an empty space, but rather a crucial center of social, political and religious interaction. In this area, the historical Babancong building, the Garut Grand Mosque, the official residence of the Regent, and the colonial monument K.F. Holle. Against the backdrop of the majestic silhouette of Mount Cikuray, this spatial layout represents a meaningful combination between the cosmological system of traditional Sundanese government and the architectural intervention of the colonial government.<br /></p>',
    'Menyaksikan_Masa_Lalu_Asal_Usul_dan_Evolusi_Kabupaten_Garut' => 'Witnessing the Past: Origins and Evolution of Garut Regency',
