    '_span_style_font_weight_bold_Arsip_Secangkir_Kopi_di_Midden_Java_span_div_a_href_https_online_fliphtml5_com_liano_Kopi_di_Midden_Java_target_blank_rel_noopener_noreferrer_style_font_weight_bold_text_decoration_line_underline_Baca_Disini_a_span_style_font_weight_bold_span_div_' => '<span style="font-weight: bold;">A Cup of Coffee in Midden Java Archives</span><div><a href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/liano/Kopi-di-Midden-Java" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline;">Read Here</a><span style="font-weight: bold;"></span></div>',
    '_span_style_font_weight_bold_Citra_Kabupaten_Tangerang_Dalam_Arsip_span_div_div_style_text_align_justify_Buku_Citra_Kabupaten_Tangerang_dalam_Arsip_ini_merupakan_naskah_sumber_yang_menyajikan_rekonstruksi_sejarah_Kabupaten_Tangerang_melalui_pemanfaatan_khazanah_arsip_sebagai_sumber_primer_utama_Buku_ini_menelusuri_dinamika_perkembangan_wilayah_Tangerang_dari_masa_prasejarah_periode_Hindu_Buddha_masa_Islam_masa_kolonial_VOC_dan_pemerintahan_Hindia_Belanda_hingga_periode_pendudukan_Jepang_revolusi_kemerdekaan_dan_masa_Republik_Indonesia_Dengan_memanfaatkan_berbagai_jenis_arsip_seperti_arsip_tekstual_arsip_foto_serta_arsip_kartografi_yang_tersimpan_di_Arsip_Nasional_Republik_Indonesia_ANRI_dan_Lembaga_Kearsipan_Daerah_Kabupaten_Tangerang_buku_ini_menampilkan_citra_Kabupaten_Tangerang_dalam_berbagai_aspek_kehidupan_meliputi_kondisi_geografis_politik_dan_pemerintahan_infrastruktur_dan_transportasi_sosial_budaya_keagamaan_pendidikan_perekonomian_hingga_pariwisata_Penyusunan_buku_ini_bertujuan_untuk_memperkaya_historiografi_lokal_sekaligus_menyediakan_landasan_evidensial_bagi_penelitian_sejarah_serta_meningkatkan_akses_masyarakat_terhadap_khazanah_arsip_sebagai_sumber_pengetahuan_dan_memori_kolektif_daerah_div_div_br_div_div_a_href_https_online_fliphtml5_com_liano_yvbn_target_blank_rel_noopener_noreferrer_style_font_weight_bold_text_decoration_line_underline_Baca_Selengkapnya_a_div_div_' => '<span style="font-weight: bold;">Image of Tangerang Regency in the Archives</span><div><div style="text-align: justify;">The book Image of Tangerang Regency in the Archives is a source text that presents a reconstruction of the history of Tangerang Regency through the use of archival treasures as the main primary source. This book traces the dynamics of the development of the Tangerang region from prehistoric times, the Hindu-Buddhist period, the Islamic period, the VOC colonial period and the Dutch East Indies government, to the period of Japanese occupation, the independence revolution and the Republic of Indonesia period. By utilizing various types of archives, such as textual archives, photo archives, and cartographic archives stored at the National Archives of the Republic of Indonesia (ANRI) and the Tangerang Regency Regional Archives Institute, this book displays the image of Tangerang Regency in various aspects of life, including geographical conditions, politics and government, infrastructure and transportation, social culture, religion, education, economy, and tourism. The preparation of this book aims to enrich local historiography as well as provide an evidentiary basis for historical research and increase public access to archival treasures as a source of knowledge and collective regional memory.',
    '_span_style_font_weight_bold_Citra_Kabupaten_Karawang_dalam_Arsip_span_div_span_style_font_weight_bold_br_span_div_div_a_href_https_online_fliphtml5_com_liano_Karawang_target_blank_rel_noopener_noreferrer_style_font_weight_bold_text_decoration_line_underline_Baca_Disini_a_div_' => '<span style="font-weight: bold;">The Image of Karawang Regency in the Archives</span><div><span style="font-weight: bold;"><br></span></div><div><a href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/liano/Karawang" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline;">Read Here</a></div>',
    '_span_style_font_weight_bold_Arsip_Banjir_Batavia_Memori_Bencana_di_Tanah_Betawi_span_div_style_text_align_justify_Buku_Naskah_Sumber_Arsip_Banjir_Batavia_Memori_Bencana_di_Tanah_Betawi_menghadirkan_rekam_jejak_historis_banjir_di_Jakarta_sejak_masa_kerajaan_kuno_era_VOC_dan_Hindia_Belanda_hingga_periode_Republik_Indonesia_Melalui_arsip_tekstual_peta_kartografi_foto_serta_dokumen_kebijakan_yang_tersimpan_di_Arsip_Nasional_Republik_Indonesia_ANRI_buku_ini_menelusuri_bagaimana_banjir_menjadi_peristiwa_berulang_yang_membentuk_wajah_kota_Batavia_Jakarta_selama_berabad_abad_Disusun_secara_tematis_dan_kronologis_buku_ini_tidak_hanya_merekam_kejadian_banjir_tetapi_juga_memperlihatkan_dinamika_tata_kota_pembangunan_kanal_kebijakan_pengendalian_air_hingga_respons_pemerintah_dan_masyarakat_dalam_menghadapi_bencana_Arsip_arsip_yang_disajikan_menunjukkan_bahwa_banjir_bukan_semata_fenomena_alam_melainkan_persoalan_struktural_yang_berkaitan_erat_dengan_perencanaan_ruang_pertumbuhan_kota_dan_perubahan_lingkungan_Sebagai_naskah_sumber_arsip_buku_ini_menempatkan_dokumen_sebagai_bukti_utama_sehingga_pembaca_dapat_memahami_persoalan_banjir_Jakarta_melalui_data_autentik_lintas_generasi_Kehadirannya_diharapkan_menjadi_rujukan_akademik_bahan_refleksi_kebijakan_sekaligus_pengingat_bahwa_pemahaman_historis_berbasis_arsip_merupakan_fondasi_penting_dalam_merumuskan_strategi_mitigasi_banjir_yang_lebih_efektif_dan_berkelanjutan_di_masa_depan_div_div_style_text_align_justify_br_div_div_style_text_align_justify_a_href_https_online_fliphtml5_com_liano_hzem_target_blank_rel_noopener_noreferrer_style_font_weight_bold_text_decoration_line_underline_Baca_Selengkapnya_a_div_' => '<span style="font-weight: bold;">Batavia Flood Archives: Memories of the Disaster in Tanah Betawi</span><div style="text-align: justify;">Manuscript Book Archive Source: Batavia Floods - Memories of the Disaster in Tanah Betawi presents a historical track record of floods in Jakarta from the time of the ancient kingdom, the era of the VOC and the Dutch East Indies, to the period of the Republic of Indonesia. Through textual archives, cartographic maps, photographs and policy documents stored in the National Archives of the Republic of Indonesia (ANRI), this book explores how floods became a recurring event that shaped the face of the city of Batavia–Jakarta for centuries. Arranged thematically and chronologically, this book not only records flood events, but also shows the dynamics of urban planning, canal construction, water control policies, and government and community responses in facing disasters. The archives presented show that flooding is not just a natural phenomenon, but a structural problem that is closely related to spatial planning, urban growth and environmental change. As an archival source text, this book places documents as the main evidence, so that readers can understand the Jakarta flood problem through authentic data across generations. It is hoped that its presence will become an academic reference, material for policy reflection, as well as a reminder that archive-based historical understanding is an important foundation in formulating more effective and sustainable flood mitigation strategies in the future.</div><div style="text-align: justify;"><br></div><div style="text-align: justify;"><a href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/liano/hzem" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline;">Read More</a></div>',
    '_span_style_font_weight_bold_Jejak_Ibu_Kota_Negara_dari_Batavia_ke_Nusantara_span_div_style_text_align_justify_Buku_Naskah_Sumber_Arsip_Jejak_Ibu_Kota_Negara_Dari_Batavia_ke_Nusantara_menghadirkan_rekaman_autentik_perjalanan_sejarah_penetapan_dan_perpindahan_ibu_kota_negara_Indonesia_sejak_masa_kolonial_hingga_era_kontemporer_Melalui_arsip_tekstual_foto_dan_peta_yang_tersimpan_di_Arsip_Nasional_Republik_Indonesia_ANRI_buku_ini_menelusuri_dinamika_kebijakan_ibu_kota_sebagai_bagian_dari_perjalanan_panjang_sejarah_bangsa_Narasi_dimulai_dari_Batavia_sebagai_pusat_pemerintahan_VOC_dan_Hindia_Belanda_pergeseran_pusat_administrasi_ke_Weltevreden_serta_wacana_pemindahan_ke_Buitenzorg_dan_Bandung_pada_masa_kolonial_Buku_ini_juga_mengangkat_momentum_krusial_masa_revolusi_ketika_ibu_kota_Republik_Indonesia_berpindah_dari_Jakarta_ke_Yogyakarta_dan_Bukittinggi_demi_mempertahankan_kedaulatan_negara_Pada_periode_pascakemerdekaan_berbagai_wacana_pemindahan_ibu_kota_ke_Palangka_Raya_dan_Jonggol_turut_dihadirkan_melalui_bukti_arsip_kebijakan_Bagian_akhir_buku_menyoroti_kebijakan_pemindahan_ibu_kota_dari_Jakarta_ke_Nusantara_di_Kalimantan_Timur_sebagai_bagian_dari_transformasi_pembangunan_nasional_Seluruh_arsip_disajikan_secara_dokumentatif_dan_kronologis_dengan_intervensi_penulis_yang_minimal_sehingga_pembaca_dapat_memahami_dinamika_penetapan_ibu_kota_melalui_bukti_sejarah_yang_otentik_dan_berimbang_Sebagai_karya_naskah_sumber_arsip_buku_ini_tidak_hanya_menjadi_rujukan_akademik_tetapi_juga_sarana_literasi_publik_untuk_memahami_bahwa_kebijakan_ibu_kota_negara_merupakan_proses_historis_yang_panjang_kompleks_dan_selalu_berkaitan_erat_dengan_dinamika_politik_ekonomi_pertahanan_serta_kedaulatan_bangsa_div_div_style_text_align_justify_br_div_div_style_text_align_justify_a_href_https_online_fliphtml5_com_liano_tfnv_target_blank_rel_noopener_noreferrer_style_font_weight_bold_text_decoration_line_underline_Baca_Selengkapnya_a_div_' => '<span style="font-weight: bold;">Traces of the National Capital from Batavia to the Archipelago</span><div style="text-align: justify;">Manuscript Book Archive Source: Traces of the National Capital - From Batavia to the Archipelago presents an authentic recording of the historical journey of the establishment and movement of the Indonesian capital from the colonial era to the contemporary era. Through textual archives, photos and maps stored in the National Archives of the Republic of Indonesia (ANRI), this book explores the dynamics of capital city policy as part of the nation\'s long history. The narrative starts from Batavia as the center of VOC government and the Dutch East Indies, the shift of the administrative center to Weltevreden, as well as the discourse of moving to Buitenzorg and Bandung during the colonial period. This book also highlights the crucial momentum of the revolutionary period when the capital of the Republic of Indonesia moved from Jakarta to Yogyakarta and Bukittinggi in order to maintain the country\'s sovereignty. In the post-independence period, various discourses on moving the capital to Palangka Raya and Jonggol were also presented through policy archive evidence. The final part of the book highlights the policy of moving the capital city from Jakarta to the archipelago in East Kalimantan as part of the national development transformation. All archives are presented in a documentary and chronological manner, with minimal author intervention, so that readers can understand the dynamics of determining the capital city through authentic and balanced historical evidence. As a manuscript work from archival sources, this book is not only an academic reference, but also a means of public literacy to understand that national capital policy is a long, complex historical process, and is always closely related to political, economic, defense and national sovereignty dynamics.</div><div style="text-align: justify;"><br></div><div style="text-align: justify;"><a href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/liano/tfnv/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline;">Read More</a></div>',
